WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.200
In the Bhagavad Gita, Krishna gives
a warrior a striking piece of advice.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.920
Let right deeds be thy motive, not
the fruit which comes from them.

3
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:15.450
In 1785, the philosopher Immanuel
Kant said something that sounds close:

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.980
only a good will acting
from duty has moral worth.

5
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.680
So is Hindu ethics simply Kantian?

6
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.460
Or is it something else?

7
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.320
In this mission, you'll set Hindu
moral principles beside Kant,

8
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.480
Bentham and virtue ethics.

9
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.860
Then you'll test them on hard
cases from the Mahabharata:

10
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.810
a lie, a deadly truth,
and a theft in a famine.

11
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.730
Your mission: weigh up whether doing your
duty without craving reward makes Hindu

12
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.120
ethics Kantian.
